      "writtenOn": "2026-06-16T21:01:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "that is a good point, I was wondering whether falling back to the `fontFace-\u003eGetMetrics()` was a good idea.\n\n\nadding @egdaniel@google.com  to this thread\n\nSome questions to follow up with for this CL\n* If `GetGDICompatibleMetrics` fails, should we fall back to `fontFace-\u003eGetMetrics()`?\n* If we fall back, should we alert the caller about doing so or fallback silently (unless in debug mode)?\n* If we choose to alert the caller, should we convert `SkScalerContext_DW::generateFontMetrics` into a boolean function such that we can return if `metrics` was initialized\n\nLet me know what you folks think. If more context is needed I can look more into the history of `SkScalerContext_DW` and let you know what I find.",
      "parentUuid": "eca0df18_ab216642",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1864,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 1864,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "253701c3a9a7eb403e04641ed47097f77cb74ea8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "59dbd9f6_d19470b0",
        "filename": "src/ports/SkScalerContext_win_dw.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 1864,
