      "writtenOn": "2026-06-16T21:16:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I looked at the other `SkScalerContext` children and they seem to be doing some early returning as well\n\nHere is an example from void SkScalerContext_GDI::generateFontMetrics(SkFontMetrics* metrics) {\n```C++\n    uint32_t ret \u003d GetOutlineTextMetrics(fDDC, sizeof(otm), \u0026otm);\n    if (0 \u003d\u003d ret) {\n        LogFontTypeface::EnsureAccessible(this-\u003egetTypeface());\n        ret \u003d GetOutlineTextMetrics(fDDC, sizeof(otm), \u0026otm);\n    }\n    if (0 \u003d\u003d ret) {\n        return;\n    }\n\n```\n\nI guess we should follow suit then, and if `GetGDICompatibleMetrics` fails just return 0s",
      "parentUuid": "59dbd9f6_d19470b0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1864,
        "startChar": 28,
